  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.52.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: libuv\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/libuv/libuv/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 478baf2599bfbc882c355288c9cb6f92e0e7dda435fa04031fa5b607cf3f414c\n  patches:\n    # linux.c:1638:21: error: 'CLOCK_BOOTTIME' undeclared\n    - boottime.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - if: unix\n      then:\n        - automake\n        - autoconf\n        - libtool\n        - make\n        - sed\n        - cmake-no-system\n        - ninja\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage('libuv', upper_bound='x') }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      include:\n        - uv.h\n      lib:\n        - uv\n      files:\n        exists:\n          - if: osx\n            then: lib/libuv.1.dylib\n          - if: linux\n            then: lib/libuv.so.1\n          - if: win\n            then:\n              - Library/lib/pkgconfig/libuv.pc\n              - Library/lib/uv.lib\n            else: lib/pkgconfig/libuv.pc\n        not_exists:\n          - lib/libuv.a\n\nabout:\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Cross-platform asynchronous I/O\n  description: |\n    libuv is a multi-platform support library with a focus on asynchronous I/O.\n    It was primarily developed for use by Node.js, but it's also used by Luvit,\n    Julia, pyuv, and others.\n  homepage: http://libuv.org/\n  repository: https://github.com/libuv/libuv\n  documentation: http://docs.libuv.org/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jjerphan\n    - frol\n    - mariusvniekerk\n    - xhochy\n",
